  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nLDAP authentication fails at the \"Retrieving user groups\" stage for users whose Distinguished Name (DN) contains non-ASCII characters (e.g., Cyrillic, Polish diacritics, etc.).\n\nUsers with ASCII-only DN authenticate successfully. Users with Unicode characters in CN receive `CredentialsSignin` error immediately after \"Retrieving user groups\" log message.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Configure Homarr with LDAP authentication against Active Directory\n2. Attempt to log in with a user whose CN contains non-ASCII characters (e.g., `CN=\u0413\u0440\u043e\u043c\u043e\u0432 \u0418\u0432\u0430\u043d,OU=Users,DC=example,DC=com`)\n3. Authentication fails with CredentialsSignin error\n\n4. Create a test user with ASCII-only CN (e.g., `CN=Test User,OU=Users,DC=example,DC=com`)\n5. Attempt to log in with this user\n6. Authentication succeeds\n\n### Impact\n\nI could use OIDC, but I'm mostly using LDAP.\n\n### Additional information\n\n## Configuration\n\n```yaml\nenvironment:\n  - AUTH_PROVIDERS=ldap\n  - AUTH_LDAP_URI=ldap://dc.example.com:389\n  - AUTH_LDAP_BASE=DC=example,DC=com\n  - AUTH_LDAP_BIND_DN=CN=service.account,OU=Services,DC=example,DC=com\n  - AUTH_LDAP_BIND_PASSWORD=***\n  - AUTH_LDAP_USERNAME_ATTRIBUTE=sAMAccountName\n  - AUTH_LDAP_USER_MAIL_ATTRIBUTE=mail\n  - AUTH_LDAP_GROUP_CLASS=group\n  - AUTH_LDAP_GROUP_MEMBER_ATTRIBUTE=member\n  - AUTH_LDAP_GROUP_MEMBER_USER_ATTRIBUTE=distinguishedName\n  - AUTH_LDAP_SEARCH_SCOPE=sub\n```\n\n## Logs\n\n### Failed authentication (user with Cyrillic CN):\n\n```\ninfo: User is trying to log in using LDAP. Connecting to LDAP server... module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"i.gromov\"\ninfo: Connected to LDAP server. Searching for user... module=\"ldapAuthorization\"\ninfo: User found in LDAP. Logging in... module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"i.gromov\"\ninfo: User credentials are correct. Retrieving user groups... module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"i.gromov\"\nerror: Read more at https://errors.authjs.dev#credentialssignin module=\"authConfiguration\" name=\"E\" type=\"CredentialsSignin\" kind=\"signIn\" code=\"credentials\"\n```\n\n### Successful authentication (user with ASCII CN):\n\n```\ninfo: User is trying to log in using LDAP. Connecting to LDAP server... module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"test.user\"\ninfo: Connected to LDAP server. Searching for user... module=\"ldapAuthorization\"\ninfo: User found in LDAP. Logging in... module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"test.user\"\ninfo: User credentials are correct. Retrieving user groups... module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"test.user\"\ninfo: User groups retrieved module=\"ldapAuthorization\" userName=\"test.user\" groups=\"1\"\ninfo: User logged in module=\"authEvents\" userId=\"...\" userName=\"test.user\"\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nUsers with non-ASCII characters in their Distinguished Name should be able to authenticate successfully, as the LDAP protocol supports UTF-8 encoded strings per RFC 4511.\n\n## Root cause hypothesis\n\nThe user's DN is used in the LDAP group membership query (`AUTH_LDAP_GROUP_MEMBER_USER_ATTRIBUTE=distinguishedName`). Non-ASCII characters in the DN are likely not being properly escaped or encoded when constructing the LDAP search filter, causing the query to fail silently.\n\n## Workaround\n\nCurrently using `credentials` provider alongside LDAP to create local accounts for affected users:\n```yaml\n- AUTH_PROVIDERS=ldap,credentials\n```\n\n## Additional context\n\n- Tested with both LDAP (port 389) and LDAPS (port 636) \u2014 same result\n- The `mail` attribute is populated for affected users (verified via LDAP browser)\n- User search works correctly (user is found and credentials are validated)\n- Only the group retrieval phase fails\n- This affects any Active Directory environment with non-English user names (Russian, Polish, Chinese, Arabic, etc.)\n\n### Version\n\n1.49.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nChrome",
